   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the issuance of\nspecialty plates for retired members of the New York state legislature",
    "basePrintNo": "S8761",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8761-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §404-ee, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8761\n\nSPONSOR: GRIFFO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the issuance\nof specialty plates for retired members of the New York state legisla-\nture\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow retired members of the legislature, while residing in the\nstate, to purchase a distinctive license plate bearing the words\n\"Retired NYS Legislator.\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 sets the provisions by which a retired member of the New York\nState Legislature may purchase a distinctive license plate. In addition\nto being a retired member of the Legislature, a member must not have\nbeen found guilty of violating the public officers law.\n\nSection 2 describes the establishment of a distinctive license plate.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nServing in elective office is an honor and a privilege; the ability to\nrepresent the people of the state of New York is significant and humbl-\ning. This bill would honor the service of retired members of the state\nLegislature by allowing them to purchase, at their own expense, a\ndistinctive license plate bearing the words \"Retired NYS Legislator\"\ncommemorating their commitment to serve their district and the state.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTBD\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall have become law.\n",
