    "lawCode": "Add §404-z, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8761A\n\nSPONSOR: GRIFFO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to the issuance of specialty plates for retired members of the\nNew York state legislature\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow retired members of the legislature, while residing in the\nstate, to purchase a distinctive license plate bearing the words\n\"Retired NYS Legislator.\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one sets the provisions by which a retired member of the New\nYork State Legislature may purchase a distinctive license plate. In\naddition to being a retired member of the Legislature, a member must not\nhave been found guilty of a felony or misdemeanor, which had a direct\nand actual relationship to the performance of such applicant's existing\nduties during the time in which he or she was a public officer.\n\nSection two describes the establishment of a distinctive license plate.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nServing in elective office is an honor and a privilege; the ability to\nrepresent the people of the state of New York is significant and humbl-\ning. This bill would honor the service of retired members of the state\nLegislature by allowing them to purchase, at their own expense, a\ndistinctive license plate bearing the words \"Retired NYS Legislator\"\ncommemorating their commitment to serve their district and the state.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n180 days.\n",
